<refentry id="systemd-init" conditional="STANDALONE_BINARIES"
    xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">

  <refentryinfo>
    <title>systemd-init</title>
    <productname>systemd</productname>
  </refentryinfo>

  <refmeta>
    <refentrytitle>systemd-init</refentrytitle>
    <manvolnum>8</manvolnum>
  </refmeta>

  <refnamediv>
    <refname>systemd-init</refname>
    <refname>init</refname>
    <refpurpose>minimal PID 1 that starts the system manager</refpurpose>
  </refnamediv>

  <refsynopsisdiv>
    <cmdsynopsis>
      <command>/usr/lib/systemd/systemd-init</command>
      <arg choice="opt" rep="repeat">OPTIONS</arg>
      <arg choice="opt">--</arg>
      <arg choice="opt" rep="repeat">MANAGER_ARGS</arg>
    </cmdsynopsis>
  </refsynopsisdiv>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Description</title>

    <para><command>systemd-init</command> is a minimal PID 1 intended to remain
    small and stable. It spawns the system manager <command>systemd-smd</command>,
    forwards signals to it, reaps children, and coordinates shutdown.</para>

    <para>This binary is built when <option>-Dstandalone-binaries=true</option>
    is enabled. In that configuration, the main system manager binary is
    <command>systemd-smd</command>, and <command>systemd-init</command> becomes
    PID 1.</para>

    <para>When invoked as <command>init</command> or <command>telinit</command> by
    a non-PID1 process (and when SysV compatibility is enabled),
    <command>systemd-init</command> execs <command>systemctl</command>, matching
    traditional SysV behavior.</para>
  </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Options</title>

    <variablelist>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><option>--shutdown-timeout=SECONDS</option></term>
        <listitem><para>Maximum time to wait for the manager to exit after a
        shutdown signal (<literal>SIGTERM</literal>, <literal>SIGINT</literal>,
        <literal>SIGPWR</literal>). The default is 90 seconds.</para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>

      <varlistentry>
        <term><option>--on-manager-exit=MODE</option></term>
        <listitem><para>Action when the manager exits unexpectedly (without a
        shutdown signal). <replaceable>MODE</replaceable> may be
        <literal>reboot</literal>, <literal>poweroff</literal>,
        <literal>halt</literal>, <literal>respawn</literal>, or
        <literal>freeze</literal>. The default is <literal>reboot</literal>.</para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>

      <varlistentry>
        <term><option>--config=PATH</option></term>
        <listitem><para>Read configuration from the specified file instead of
        <filename>/etc/systemd/init.conf</filename>.</para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
  </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Configuration</title>

    <para><command>systemd-init</command> reads
    <filename>/etc/systemd/init.conf</filename> by default. The file contains
    simple <literal>KEY=VALUE</literal> pairs. Supported keys are:</para>

    <variablelist>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><varname>ShutdownTimeoutSec</varname></term>
        <listitem><para>Override the shutdown wait timeout in seconds.</para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><varname>OnManagerExit</varname></term>
        <listitem><para>Set the unexpected manager exit policy. Accepted values
        are the same as <option>--on-manager-exit=</option>.</para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
  </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Files</title>
    <variablelist>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><filename>/usr/lib/systemd/systemd-init</filename></term>
        <listitem><para>Minimal PID 1 binary.</para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><filename>/usr/lib/systemd/systemd-smd</filename></term>
        <listitem><para>System manager spawned by <command>systemd-init</command>.</para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term><filename>/etc/systemd/init.conf</filename></term>
        <listitem><para>Configuration file.</para></listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
  </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
    <title>See Also</title>
    <para>
      <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>,
      <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-system.conf</refentrytitle><manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry>,
      <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemctl</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>
    </para>
  </refsect1>

</refentry>
